# Open G Slide Blues (repertoire plan: st-open-g-slide). An original 12-bar blues in G for
# slide guitar in open G tuning: strings 6 to 1 tuned D G D G B D (D2 G2 D3 G3 B3 D4). From
# standard tuning, tune strings 6, 5 and 1 down a whole step (E to D, A to G, E to D).
# The slide is on finger 3 (or 4). Touch the string right over the fret wire, never press it
# down. Fingers 1 and 2 rest lightly on the strings behind the slide so they do not ring or
# buzz, and the picking hand mutes the strings you are not playing.
# Every fret number is a fret in open G. Across the strings, fret 12 is a G chord, fret 5 a
# C chord and fret 7 a D chord: the three chords of the blues. On the top three strings:
#   string 1 (D4): 5 G4, 7 A4, 8 Bb4, 10 C5, 12 D5, 15 F5
#   string 2 (B3): 5 E4, 7 F#4, 8 G4, 11 Bb4, 12 B4, 15 D5
#   string 3 (G3): 5 C4, 7 D4, 10 F4, 12 G4
# The whole-chord slides sound plain G, C and D; the single-note answers add each chord's flat
# seventh (F over G, Bb over C, C over D), so the harmony is G7, C7 and D7. The blue note
# Bb4 (string 2, fret 11) slides up into B4 in bars 2 and 8.
# Swing: each beat is long-short, written as a triplet quarter (q3) then a triplet eighth (e3).
title: Open G Slide Blues
